{
  "result": "If I had to pick just one, I'd make sure every kid grows up feeling safe, seen, and loved.\n\nNot in a perfect, utopian way \u2014 just basically. Fed, protected, and with at least one person who truly believes in them, and the freedom to be curious without being afraid.\n\nIt sounds small compared to ending war or solving climate change, but I think so much of what goes wrong later traces back to that start. Adults who were hurt, lonely, or scared as kids are more likely to be anxious, angry, addicted, or closed off as adults. And adults who felt secure are more likely to be trusting, generous, and creative.\n\nChange that first chapter for everyone, and you don\u2019t just get happier people \u2014 you get a completely different world downstream: less cruelty, less fear-driven politics, more curiosity, more ability to actually take care of each other.\n\nI wouldn\u2019t make everyone the same, or remove all suffering. I\u2019d just remove the kind that comes from never feeling like you matter to anyone.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
